\ul{
\li{Conversion and everything it triggers is 37 to 42 \% of the workers' CPU, and five sixths of that is under the comparison of the arguments of two applications. Inside conversion the mixture is the general one (on Mathlib: hash consing 21 \%, conversion's own code 18 \%, memo lookups 17 \%, levels 11 \%, evaluation 9 \%, the term store 8 \%, code blocks 7 \%).}
\li{Lazy delta reduction is on the stack of 17 \% of the samples on all three corpora; a running code block of 9 to 14 \%.}
\li{Proof irrelevance, which was 27.5 \% of the workers' CPU in rep-P10, is 0.8 to 1.7 \%.}
}
}

