\ul{
\li{\strong{The probes are instruction-bound, as before}: closures, frames and neutral applications run at 4.5 to 4.7 instructions per cycle with 7 to 12 \% of their cycles stalled. A layout change cannot make them faster; only fewer probes can.}
\li{\strong{The memory-bound items are the same as in rep-P10}: universe levels (2.26 instructions per cycle, 38 \% of their cycles stalled, 18 \% of all last-level misses and 22 \% of all TLB walks for 5 \% of the instructions), the inline caches and block lookup of code blocks (29 \% stalled), proof-block decoding (29 \%), table growth (23 \%), the kernel (29 \%).}
\li{\strong{TLB walks are not an item}: 301 million per two passes; at 30 cycles each that is 1.2 \% of the workers' cycles.}
}
}

